  <static seed="1882" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionApplication/FractionSubtractionWordProblems20.pg">
    <statement><p>Priscilla is participating in a running event. In the first hour, she completed <m>{{\frac{2}{9}}}</m> of the total distance. After another hour, in total she had completed <m>{{\frac{32}{63}}}</m> of the total distance.</p>
<p>What fraction of the total distance did Priscilla complete during the second hour?</p>
<p>Priscilla completed <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> of the distance during the second hour.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{2}{7}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>This is a subtraction problem.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}[t]
   {{\frac{32}{63}}} - {{\frac{2}{9}}} 
      \amp = \frac{32}{63}-\frac{2 \cdot 7}{9 \cdot 7} \\
      \amp = \frac{32}{63} - \frac{14}{63} \\
      \amp = \frac{32-14}{63} \\
      \amp = \frac{18}{63} \\
      \amp = {{\frac{2}{7}}}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>Priscilla completed <m>{{\frac{2}{7}}}</m> of the distance during the second hour.</p>
</solution>
